"use strict";(self.webpackChunk=self.webpackChunk||[]).push([[705],{9122:(e,t,n)=>{n.r(t),n.d(t,{data:()=>i});const i={key:"v-0d1f3edc",path:"/WIP_slot1-launch.html",title:"",lang:"en-US",frontmatter:{},excerpt:"",headers:[{level:2,title:"TWiLight Menu++",slug:"twilight-menu",children:[]}],filePathRelative:"WIP_slot1-launch.md",git:{updatedTime:1635103736e3,contributors:[{name:"Pk11",email:"epicpkmn11@outlook.com",commits:1}]}}},9942:(e,t,n)=>{n.r(t),n.d(t,{default:()=>l});const i=(0,n(6252).uE)('<p>The Nintendo DSi has a Slot-1 cartridge slot, and the Nintendo DSi System Menu has a built in Slot-1 launcher. However, not only does it block out unlicensed cartridges but many alternative Slot-1 launchers have additional benefits. These include expanding the VRAM bus to 32-bit (making 32-bit read/writes faster), boosting the CPU to 133 MHz, enabling internal SD card access (for homebrew) alongside other advantages.</p><p>However, compatibility isn&#39;t always so spot-on and whether titles boot or not depend on which Slot-1 launcher you use.</p><p>You will need to have Unlaunch installed to use custom Slot-1 launchers.</p><h2 id="twilight-menu" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#twilight-menu" aria-hidden="true">#</a> TWiLight Menu++</h2><p>TWiLight Menu++&#39;s Slot-1 launcher comes with all the above improvements and is the recommended Slot-1 launcher to use. While not offering cheat support, it offers support for all of the advantages listed above.</p><ol><li>Turn on your Nintendo DSi while <kbd class="face">A</kbd> &amp; <kbd class="face">B</kbd> are held <ul><li>This should take you to Unlaunch&#39;s Filemenu</li></ul></li><li>Launch <code>sd:/_nds/twilightmenu/settings.srldr</code></li><li>Switch over to the &quot;Misc</li></ol>',6),o={},l=(0,n(3744).Z)(o,[["render",function(e,t){return i}]])},3744:(e,t)=>{t.Z=(e,t)=>{for(const[n,i]of t)e[n]=i;return e}}}]);